One thing this run does not demonstrate, said plainly rather than left to be
inferred: the Etherfuse pool held nothing at the time, so deployed_capital and
the PC_NAV exposure were the same 100000000 and the old formula would have paid
the same 1897996. The divergence between the two formulas is demonstrated in
scripts/e2e-etherfuse.sh step 5, where the Etherfuse pool holds 1000000000 and
appears as a line of its own priced from EF_BOND, and it is what produced the
26 October error: 36357814 paid where 21033446 was owed.
